WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.223
Grandpa put six big sweet potatoes into a sack for Mr. Henderson.

2
00:00:09.224 --> 00:00:14.981
"Two dollars and fifty cents!" said Katie. "And thank you!"

3
00:00:14.982 --> 00:00:19.513
"I’d like three squashes," said Mr. Dexter.

4
00:00:19.514 --> 00:00:22.990
Today was the Willow Creek Harvest Fair.

5
00:00:22.991 --> 00:00:28.845
The whole Donovan family was helping Grandpa sell his garden produce.

6
00:00:28.846 --> 00:00:36.034
Squashes, onions, carrots, apples, radishes, and turnips covered Grandpa’s table.

7
00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:39.519
A dozen fat pumpkins sat on the ground.

8
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.542
"Could someone carry a pumpkin to my car?" asked Mrs. Pinker.

9
00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:49.021
"I’d like three apples," said Jeff the mailman.

10
00:00:49.022 --> 00:00:52.946
"How much are your turnips?" asked Mrs. Penkov.

11
00:00:52.947 --> 00:00:57.416
"Where is Joy?" said Mom. "We need help!"

12
00:00:57.417 --> 00:01:02.148
"I saw her over there just a minute ago," said Mr. Henderson.

13
00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:05.481
"She’s listening to the country band."

14
00:01:05.482 --> 00:01:09.287
"Katie, run and get her," said Mom.

15
00:01:09.288 --> 00:01:12.791
Katie ran through the crowd in the town park.

16
00:01:12.792 --> 00:01:17.682
She found her sister bouncing to the beat of loud country music.

17
00:01:17.683 --> 00:01:19.983
"Joy!" called Katie.

18
00:01:19.984 --> 00:01:24.168
"Mom said to come help at the produce stand!"

19
00:01:24.169 --> 00:01:27.788
Joy was not paying attention to her sister.

20
00:01:27.789 --> 00:01:33.149
When the band played their final notes, she clapped and cheered with the crowd.

21
00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:36.913
Then a girl in jean overalls ran onto the stage.

22
00:01:36.914 --> 00:01:40.011
She was carrying a violin.

23
00:01:40.012 --> 00:01:48.617
"Let’s all welcome this little fiddler from Kirbyville—Maggie Dowell!" shouted the announcer. "Look!

24
00:01:48.618 --> 00:01:52.543
She’s our age," Joy said. Katie

25
00:01:52.544 --> 00:01:59.045
watched as Maggie Dowell lifted her fiddle and started playing an old folk song. At

26
00:01:59.046 --> 00:02:02.963
first she played slowly and gently. "Tell

27
00:02:02.964 --> 00:02:05.636
Mom I’ll be right there," said Joy. "I

28
00:02:05.637 --> 00:02:08.300
want to hear one more song." "Okay,"

29
00:02:08.301 --> 00:02:12.788
said Katie, but she didn’t move either. Maggie’s

30
00:02:12.789 --> 00:02:16.437
fiddle playing was getting livelier. She

31
00:02:16.438 --> 00:02:19.610
stomped her right foot to the beat. Her

32
00:02:19.611 --> 00:02:25.115
bow ripped across the strings and sent puffs of dust into the air. "I

33
00:02:25.116 --> 00:02:29.464
wish I could play the fiddle like that!" said Joy. "Come

34
00:02:29.465 --> 00:02:32.752
on, Joy," Katie reminded her sister.

35
00:02:32.753 --> 00:02:38.665
"We’re supposed to be helping Grandpa."

36
00:02:38.666 --> 00:02:46.069
Later that afternoon, the Donovans sat at a picnic table eating fried fish and corn on the cob.

37
00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:50.115
"Here comes Aunt Sally and Luke!" said Katie.

38
00:02:50.116 --> 00:02:55.661
"Larry’s dad just won the giant pumpkin contest!" said Luke.

39
00:02:55.662 --> 00:03:00.122
"His pumpkin weighed more than one hundred pounds!"

40
00:03:00.123 --> 00:03:04.850
"We sold every one of our pumpkins," said Katie.

41
00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:08.627
"Did you meet your goal?" asked Aunt Sally.

42
00:03:08.628 --> 00:03:11.291
"Yes, we did," said Grandpa.

43
00:03:11.292 --> 00:03:14.480
"We made enough to buy seeds for next year."

44
00:03:14.481 --> 00:03:18.688
"And to get the garden fence repaired," said Dad.

45
00:03:18.689 --> 00:03:22.247
Joy wasn’t interested in pumpkins or seeds.

46
00:03:22.248 --> 00:03:28.504
She could talk about only one thing—Maggie Dowell’s fiddle playing.

47
00:03:28.505 --> 00:03:32.100
"You should have heard that girl!" she said.

48
00:03:32.101 --> 00:03:35.766
"Yeah! She was great!" said Katie.

49
00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:40.772
She jumped up and wildly played an imaginary fiddle.

50
00:03:40.773 --> 00:03:45.160
Then she plopped back down and picked up her corn on the cob.

51
00:03:45.161 --> 00:03:48.373
"But who wants to practice all the time?"

52
00:03:48.374 --> 00:03:51.196
"I wouldn’t mind practicing," said Joy.

53
00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:55.219
"I’d do anything to play like Maggie Dowell."

54
00:03:55.220 --> 00:04:01.754
"Your great-grandma Donovan got her first fiddle when she was no bigger than you," said Grandpa.

55
00:04:01.755 --> 00:04:06.602
"Her daddy went all the way to Bates City and bought her a half-size one.

56
00:04:06.603 --> 00:04:08.968
It was made in Germany."

57
00:04:08.969 --> 00:04:13.253
"I wish you girls had known your great-grandma," said Dad.

58
00:04:13.254 --> 00:04:17.176
"I wish I had heard her play," said Joy.

59
00:04:17.177 --> 00:04:21.821
"Where is that fiddle?" said Grandpa. "In the attic?"

60
00:04:21.822 --> 00:04:25.408
"It might be up there," said Mom.

61
00:04:25.409 --> 00:04:27.431
Joy’s mouth fell open.

62
00:04:27.432 --> 00:04:29.667
"Do you still have it?"

63
00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:31.956
"Oh yes," said Grandpa.

64
00:04:31.957 --> 00:04:35.206
"She never sold that first little fiddle."

65
00:04:35.207 --> 00:04:38.450
"Can we look for it?" said Joy.

66
00:04:38.451 --> 00:04:42.361
"We’ll look for it tomorrow morning," said Grandpa.

67
00:04:42.362 --> 00:04:45.498
"Maybe one of you girls would like to try it."

68
00:04:45.499 --> 00:04:48.355
Katie wiped butter dripping from her chin.

69
00:04:48.356 --> 00:04:51.322
"Not me," she said.

70
00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:57.317
"Me!" said Joy.

